From fc355d4766a6dbb9511d9c5abadbcbc9d4c543df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaR4eJl <marchel666@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:46:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: reliable Ollama fallback, deterministic routing, and
 green test suite

Root causes fixed (was 22 failed / 28 passed -> 64 passed / 0 failed):

- ModelRegistry.__init__ now accepts an optional candidate iterable, so
  ModelRegistry([...]) works again (this was the "takes 1 positional
  argument but 2 were given" error breaking ~13 tests).
- router._available: providers without a required API key (local/custom
  pools) are treated as available; Anthropic stays key-or-CLI, OpenAI/
  Gemini/OpenRouter still require their key, Ollama still health-checks.
- router.rank: actually sweep and clear expired cooldowns (open -> half-open)
  from both memory and the persisted provider_health table (dead code before).
- router._persist: use setdefault so a provider's first success no longer
  raises KeyError; health/stats tables are (re)created lazily so a repointed
  db stays correct.
- OllamaAdapter: send /api/tags as a urllib Request (keeps monkeypatched
  urlopen observable) while production traffic uses the proxy-free opener so
  loopback never goes through HTTP(S)_PROXY.
- orchestrator.run: define `manager` before the executor try/except
  (UnboundLocalError when running without a JobManager).
- jobs.submit: support sub-second/float timeouts instead of flooring to 1s.
- app.py /run: re-emit job.created into the session (was dropped).
- SessionStore: in-memory session cache for consistent event replay.

Env/config: python-dotenv loaded before providers are built (already in
place); .env stays untracked via new .gitignore.

Tests: added tests/conftest.py to isolate runtime DBs per test, plus
tests/test_ollama_integration.py covering env loading, Ollama availability/
model discovery/tag-prefix match, completion, malformed/timeout/connection
errors, no-proxy transport, and Claude->Ollama weekly-limit fallback.

No public APIs, providers, roles, fallback, or circuit breaker removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
